Fillets: a blend rolling on an edge that runs into the spine's end vertex
ends there where its walk stopped with a section of no width a hair short
of the vertex (mitcad#343).

The case: 0904's notch wall narrowing to the spine's first vertex, its far
edge running into it: the blend rolls on that edge and vanishes at the
vertex. On the stored body the walk reached the vertex. On a body a few
micrometres off, its contacts met 0.005 before the vertex (a hundredth of
the radius is 0.0086) and the walk stopped there: the stripe was not
finished (its end not at the spine's end), the next step had no edge to
roll on and failed, and the stripe with it.

- ChFi3d_RollsIntoVertex: whether a side of a piece rolls on an edge that
  has the spine's end vertex.
- PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine: a walk rolling on such an edge ends the stripe
  where its contacts are within ten times the tolerance of each other and
  within a hundredth of the radius of that vertex (ContactsAtTangentEnd,
  as for a vanishing end where the faces come tangent).
- ChFi3d_RolledIntoEndVertex takes the contact on that edge within a
  hundredth of the radius of the vertex where the section has no width, so
  that PerformFilletOnVertex puts the end at the vertex (0904).

Upstream: new.

